MID_LGV_2_M04_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bel_m01_001: With Arago added to our number, there are now\nthree former imperial nations in the Alliance.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bel_m01_002: Together, we can topple the emperor, who commits\natrocity after atrocity—and thinks of us as beasts.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bel_m01_003: And we can create a world free of injustice.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Bel_m01: <BLN>Let's strike him down!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Seo_m01_001: At last we have our jaws around our enemy's throat.\nBut we cannot grow complacent.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Seo_m01_002: In battle, it is the height of folly to charge in without\na plan, cocksure in one's strength.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Seo_m01_003: When we defeat our foe soundly and claim a glorious\nvictory, it will be through careful preparation.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Seo_m01: <BLN>Make thorough preparations.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tia_m01_001: Her Highness Aswan... No, sorry, it's "Her Majesty"\nnow. I can hardly believe Arago has a new queen.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tia_m01_002: I'm praying her reign brings peace to her country.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Tia_m01: <BLN>Her Majesty Aswan...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pet_m01_001: Out of all the gods, I think Credna seems friendliest.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pet_m01_002: I feel like we'd get along pretty well, you know?
MID_LGA_2_M04_Pet_m01: <BLN>Credna seems friendly...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hur_m01_001: I saw the name Lind in an old temple record.\nLind...the Baneful Knight.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hur_m01_002: He was a legendary warrior. You'd hear his name\nalongside the demigod heroes, even. However...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hur_m01_003: The records show he used cruel methods to suppress\nrebellion. This guy was feared by friend and foe.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hur_m01_004: I'm scared of him too... I'll admit it. But I won't be\ndefeated. We're all making it home alive.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Hur_m01: <BLN>The Baneful Knight...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Max_m01_001: What the captive soldiers have told me about Lind...\nHe's so bad, even I'M shocked! Heh heh!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Max_m01_002: His allies are even more scared of him than they\nare of me!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Max_m01_003: Maybe he's doing it to scare people into obedience.\nEither way, the Lord of Impalement's one sick puppy.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Max_m01: <BLN>The Lord of Impalement...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gol_m01_001: I was never a big fan of the capital, but I'm kinda\nworried now that it's all weird.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gol_m01_002: Y'know, I got people there. Gabriel, Poloni. My old\ngladiator buddies.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gol_m01_003: I hope they're all doin' OK. And that the emperor's\nnot pickin' on 'em.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Gol_m01: <BLN>I'm kinda worried.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gat_m01_001: It's unfathomable that we've reached the capital\nmere months after our first clashes with the empire.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gat_m01_002: Brezarant's future—indeed, the continent's—is at a\ncritical tipping point.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Gat_m01_003: But I will not hesitate. I vow to Mars I'll use all my\nstrength to defeat the emperor.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Gat_m01: <BLN>This is the great tipping point.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dan_m01_001: Even from this side of the bridge, one can sense the\nchange in Dagsion's atmosphere.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dan_m01_002: Were this a cursed island from an adventure tale,\none might expect a reeking fog to emanate from it.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dan_m01_003: But it is as if an overpowering nothingness is\ncovering the capital and drifting this way.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dan_m01_004: And that reality—deafening silence—is even more\nunsettling.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Dan_m01: <BLN>Strange, isn't it?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fab_m01_001: This infighting between the children of the goddess\nis an unanticipated height of petty selfishness.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fab_m01_002: And they call themselves gods! Though, thanks to\nthis, a chance to slay a Founder has arisen.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fab_m01_003: For now, I will observe quietly. I do wonder how the\ngoddess feels just now. Heh.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Fab_m01: <BLN>Pure, petty selfishness.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Esm_m01_001: Everyone seems happy that we have gods on our\nside. I can understand that.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Esm_m01_002: But people on the empire's side believed in the gods\ntoo. And then they got betrayed.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Esm_m01_003: Faith is a scary thing, isn't it? Yeah.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Esm_m01: <BLN>We have gods on our side.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Urs_m01_001: Even with all these casualties around us, Vandahl\nTrading continues to grow.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Urs_m01_002: Many merchants and mercenaries are fleeing the\nempire and coming to us, begging to be hired.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Urs_m01_003: Thanks to that, my days have become a whirlwind of\nback-to-back interviews...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Urs_m01: <BLN>I have another interview soon...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sim_m01_001: I've been taking life ever since I was a kid.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sim_m01_002: So, until recently, when a young person died, I just\nthought it was because they were weak...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sim_m01_003: Now it's strange though. I don't want them to die.\nHuh. Must be getting soft in my old age.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Sim_m01: <BLN>Must be getting old...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lou_m01_001: Ugh... I can still smell the blood on me. War's nothing\nlike it is in stories.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lou_m01_002: I want this fight to be over, already. I'm ready for a\ndifferent adventure, you know?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lou_m01_003: Even though adventuring can be dirty, I'd take mud\nand sweat over being stained with blood any day...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Lou_m01: <BLN>I'd rather read about war...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fia_m01_001: I am...fine...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fia_m01_002: I just... I'm tired from all this crying...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fia_m01_003: I hear that King Gilchris of Arago has passed away...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Fia_m01_004: Bertrand... Why did he look at me like that when\nhe returned? Why...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Fia_m01: <BLN>...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Die_m01_001: Though not a warrior, Credna is strong in his own\nway, far more than some would think.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Die_m01_002: He shed a tear for just a moment over what's\nhappened...and then got right to work.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Die_m01_003: I too...must keep moving.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Die_m01: <BLN>I must do the same.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lor_m01_001: Ha! Now that Credna is here, everything's gonna\nbe fine!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lor_m01_002: He's smart. He makes awesome weapons. He\ncan do all sorts of great stuff!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lor_m01_003: So now I know we're going to win! I totally\nbelieve in him!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Lor_m01: <BLN>Everything's gonna be fine!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Set_m01_001: Dagda the Great, turning against his own son\nCredna and his other children...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Set_m01_002: It was inconceivable that the balance of things\ncould tip to this disastrous extent.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Set_m01_003: But this is where matters stand, so I am fully\ncommitted to seeing this battle through.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Set_m01: <BLN>Inconceivable...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nin_m01_001: Credna, Jurah, even Mars from Brezarant...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nin_m01_002: One after another, the divines are reaching out\nto the children of Damascar.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nin_m01_003: They join the fight against Dagda. I hope you're\nseeing this wherever you are, Yu Phas...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Nin_m01: <BLN>Yu Phas, wherever you are...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bon_m01_001: Why is the capital so shrouded in silence? We have\ntoo little information.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bon_m01_002: But rushing in for reconnaissance would play into the\nenemy's hands. Our operation is already in motion.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Bon_m01_003: All I can do is try to remain calm, even as my mind\nfeels like it may burst into flame from anxiety.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Bon_m01: <BLN>We have too little information...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tob_m01_001: I've been trying to picture what's going on inside the\ncapital, but it's beyond me.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tob_m01_002: Besides, nothing we can do about it until we take\ncare of that Lind guy camped out on the bridge.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tob_m01_003: If you need someone to storm his position, I'm your\nman! I'll bring back their general's head myself!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Tob_m01: <BLN>Leave it to me!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lil_m01_001: I always thought of Credna as sorta unimpressive\nfor a god.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lil_m01_002: But now that he's on our side, maybe he's got some\ngood plans or solid info.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lil_m01_003: Though I wonder if his heart is really in a fight\nagainst the empire...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lil_m01_004: I mean, Credna is Dagda the Great's own kid.\nMust be kinda weird for him.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Lil_m01: <BLN>I can't figure Credna out.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lys_m01_001: It seems that some of the Brezarant knights fight\ntogether as father and child.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Lys_m01_002: If my father had lived, perhaps I too would have...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Lys_m01: <BLN>I envy those knights...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_001: In my days as a pilus prior, I once spoke with Lord\nGuillermo about defending the imperial capital.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_004: In my days as a pilus prior, I spoke with Viceroy\nGuillermo about defending the imperial capital.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_002: We decided Dagsion was impregnable... Those were\nyounger days, of course.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_005: We decided Dagsion was impregnable... Those were\nyounger days, of course.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_003: Now, we stand here as the attacking force. And I will\nsmash through the gates.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Buc_m01_006: Now, we stand here as the attacking force. And I will\nsmash through the gates.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Buc_m01: <BLN>Impregnable, we thought.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sci_m01_001: Something foul is on the wind...although the battle\nis yet to even begin.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sci_m01_002: I sense it from the direction of Alcineus Span...\nIt concerns me.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sci_m01_003: Unless I miss my guess, this enemy general is\nruthless indeed.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Sci_m01: <BLN>A foul wind blows.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Moo_m01_001: Credna is Dagda's kid, isn't he?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Moo_m01_002: I guess there are some things you can never forgive,\neven if it's your parents doing them.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Moo_m01_003: Especially if it's evil. We've got to put a stop to his\ntyranny!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Moo_m01: <BLN>Even if they're your parents...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Mic_m01_001: Trust me, I'm glad to have gods on our side.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Mic_m01_002: You could look at it as a family quarrel...one that\nturned into a war.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Mic_m01_003: It's too late for them to talk about it, but it still hits\nme in the heart to think about it that way.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Mic_m01: <BLN>A family quarrel.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Oly_m01_001: It may surprise you to learn that I take great pleasure\nin silence.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Oly_m01_002: In silence, one has the chance to express their\nartistry, be that through music or poetry!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Oly_m01_003: But I hate this silence. It is like the silence of a\nmute audience. Indeed, a stifled audience!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Oly_m01: <BLN>I hate this.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Naz_m01_001: War takes a lot of brainpower. You need to know\nall about weapons and strategies.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Naz_m01_002: I don't get that stuff. I'm here because sometimes all\nyou need to do is go wild. That's my specialty.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Naz_m01_003: Just lemme know when it's time for me to do my\nthing. I'll leave all the thinking to you!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Naz_m01: <BLN>War takes brainpower.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sar_m01_001: When we first came here, the Heroic Games were\njust beginning. Now we've returned as invaders.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sar_m01_002: We have to do everything we can to avoid hurting\ninnocent people.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sar_m01_003: We mustn't let ourselves be as destructive as\nthe Divine Emperor. It's wrong, and I refuse.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Sar_m01: <BLN>This time we're invading.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dai_m01_001: Yeah, we won our fight with the kingdom of Arago,\nbut that city got crushed. Serious destruction there.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dai_m01_002: Now Dagsion's the battlefield, and all the people we\nmet there are going to have their lives ruined.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dai_m01_003: So I've decided that if I see any innocent person in\ntrouble, I'm going to get them to safety.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Dai_m01_004: I don't even care if everyone tries to stop me. I won't\nignore anyone who needs help.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Dai_m01: <BLN>I won't ignore anyone in trouble!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hal_m01_001: W-we've got gods in our camp. And they're talking to\nus like it's normal! They're so beautiful. So majestic.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hal_m01_002: So many big, scary things are happening now.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hal_m01_003: I wonder what will happen to all of us...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Hal_m01: <BLN>They're so beautiful!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Guj_m01_001: Well, it's come to this, has it? Saramis and\nBrezarant must be desperate.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Guj_m01_002: Asking me to train soldiers? Telling me I'd get\npaid just "sometime" in the future?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Guj_m01_003: I don't mind, I guess. I'll be in the midst of good-\nlookin' recruits—and help two nations to victory too!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Guj_m01: <BLN>I'll give 'em the best training!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Yan_m01_001: If people refuse to turn away from greed and\nfoolishness, they always go astray.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Yan_m01_002: For the gods, it's no different. At heart, they're\nmuch the same as us.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Yan_m01_003: Which is why, given the evil they've unleashed, \nthey deserve the punishment people face.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Yan_m01: <BLN>Evil must be punished!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Iio_m01_001: An Aragonian soldier handed me a letter. I was\nshocked to see that it was from my mother.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Iio_m01_002: She wrote, "Keep your eyes on what's ahead."\nGah! My parents were always light on words.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Iio_m01_003: It's a shame that I can't see her now. But I've\ndecided to waste no time on regrets.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Iio_m01: <BLN>I got a letter...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pep_m01_001: Who would have foreseen that we—who came to\nthe capital for one reason—now return for another!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pep_m01_002: We hear that all other bridges into the city, with the\nexception of Alcineus Span, have been destroyed.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pep_m01_003: We hope that all the young ones were able to flee\nDagsion before it was closed off.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Pep_m01_004: Oh, spirits... Have mercy upon the children!\nGrant your benediction to the young ones!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Pep_m01: <BLN>What twists of fate...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Noc_m01_001: I've had an uneasy feeling...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Noc_m01_002: A really bad feeling...that something beyond\nterrible is about to happen.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Noc_m01_003: I hope my hunch is wrong. I'm not the most\nclearheaded right now.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Noc_m01: <BLN>I have a bad feeling...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sop_m01_001: When you're really hungry, no matter what you\nlook at, you think, "Yes, I could eat that!"
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sop_m01_002: I wonder if there's a world where that's a real\nthing—that everything is made of food?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Sop_m01_003: You could eat absolutely everything, even the\nclouds in the sky? Ah, I can dream...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Sop_m01: <BLN>No food yet, huh...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cat_m01_001: The kingdom of Arago will be in tatters for some\ntime to come.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cat_m01_002: No doubt, there are unseemly sorts who will take\nadvantage of this. I must watch out for them.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cat_m01_003: I can't endure another tragedy on the scale of what\nhappened in Cydonia.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Cat_m01: <BLN>I must keep an eye out!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ned_m01_001: The imperial capital will certainly defend itself with\nthe finest forces from the temples.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ned_m01_002: Our soldiers must be aware of this. Some seem\nafraid of the fighting ahead.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ned_m01_003: But I, as a warrior, look forward to what's to come.\nIt will test my martial prowess to the extreme.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Ned_m01: <BLN>We must face this.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Zac_m01_001: It's the bandit's way to shake down villages\nduring war—to rob every home you can.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Zac_m01_002: But sometimes you bump into those who have\nthe same idea.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Zac_m01_003: When that happens, you've gotta scram. Gold's\nnot worth anything if you're dead.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Zac_m01: <BLN>I bet you know this.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Maj_m01_001: I hear some soldiers we've captured are getting\nthrown in prison.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Maj_m01_002: I'm used to that, but it's not easy for most people.\nStill, they better be grateful we didn't off 'em!
MID_LGA_2_M04_Maj_m01: <BLN>The soldiers we captured...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ven_m01_001: Seems that more and more soldiers aren't\ngetting decent shut-eye. That's too bad.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ven_m01_002: They're the types who'll probably find it hard to go\nback to their regular lives after all this.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ven_m01_003: A friend of mine suffered like that once. Hmm,\nwhat happened to him? Probably died...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Ven_m01: <BLN>They gotta toughen up...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ini_m01_001: Kill...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ini_m01_002: Kill... Kill...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ini_m01_003: Kill, kill, kill... Killll, killl, KILLLL...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ini_m01_004: Huh?! Oh, damn it all. It happened again...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Ini_m01: <BLN>Kill... Kill...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jas_m01_001: It's good to rescue injured soldiers. But maybe I\ntook it too far, paying for their medical costs.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jas_m01_002: Still, you can't trade a life for money. So I think\ndoing that was probably the right thing to do.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jas_m01_003: I wonder if my ol' husband would have forgiven\nme for spending my hard-earned coins like that.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Jas_m01: <BLN>Was that too much?
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ale_m01_001: I never thought the day would come when I was\ncommanded by Jurah herself.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ale_m01_002: She offered words of thanks and encouragement.\nI...nearly cried in joy.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Ale_m01_003: But I must save my tears for later, after our\nvictory. We must win this battle.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Ale_m01: <BLN>From Jurah herself...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cen_m01_001: Suppose things continue as they are. Our forces\nconquer Dagsion, and the Divine Emperor is killed...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cen_m01_002: Everything in these lands will change dramatically.\nLaws, political hierarchies... All of it.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cen_m01_003: That said, the one thing that will never change is my\nworship of Aurora.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Cen_m01: <BLN>Suppose, if...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Kir_m01_001: A young rascal I met some time ago brought me his\nlittle boat. Whole thing made me bawl.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Kir_m01_002: He said pirates play a big part in times like this.\nThen he gave me his boat, sayin' he bought it for me!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Kir_m01_003: But I can't be that rascal's captain. I dress in rags...\nGot no sail to my name... He deserves better...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Kir_m01: <BLN>I bawled like a baby...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nuz_m01_001: The chance to overthrow Dagda has come at last.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nuz_m01_002: We children of Damascar will have vengeance for\nour homeland's downfall.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Nuz_m01: <BLN>We will have vengeance!
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nat_m01_001: When Creek told me to follow my heart, I'll admit\nthat I wavered.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nat_m01_002: His words pierced me deeply.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nat_m01_003: Perhaps all this time, I've been ignoring what my\nheart tells me.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Nat_m01_004: But I'll listen once again... I'll find a cause worth\nmore to me than national loyalty.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Nat_m01: <BLN>Follow my heart.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hri_m01_001: There were some things I never saw until I stepped\nout of my homeland's perspective.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hri_m01_002: Knighthood is a path of loyalty. But in challenging\nthe emperor, you all walk the path of humanity.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Hri_m01_003: Humanity, too, needs knights to succeed. So I\nwill walk this path now.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Hri_m01: <BLN>The meaning of loyalty...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tro_m01_001: I know everyone is tired after crossing the desert,\nbut I'm afraid there's little time to catch our breath.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Tro_m01_002: Something foul is going on in Dagsion. I don't like\nwhat the signs suggest.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Tro_m01: <BLN>No time to catch our breath.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cla_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cla_m01_001: I never imagined I'd return to Dagsion in this\nmanner.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Cla_m01_002: Had I only foreseen this situation, I would have\ncreated secret ways into the city.
MID_LGA_2_M04_Cla_m01: <BLN>I never imagined...
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01_001: I am...terrified of the Divine Emperor.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01_002: As his wife, I still love him. But my fear of him\nis stronger.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01_003: He was not always this wicked...though his\ntemperament was often abrasive.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01_004: Thinking back...he began to decline when Magistra\nRaksha started supplying him with flamma.
MID_LGV_2_M04_Jun_m01_005: His personality has grown cruel and merciless...
MID_LGA_2_M04_Jun_m01: <BLN>Dagda is a cruel man...
MID_LGV_2_M04_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B01_m01_001: Aww... I'm getting reassigned out of my\ngirlfriend's unit.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B01_m01_002: I'm jealous of her pegasus. It gets to be with her way\nmore than I do.
MID_LGA_2_M04_B01_m01: <BLN>Aww...
MID_LGV_2_M04_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B02_m01_001: It was a little more than a year ago when I marched\nin Her Majesty's entrance procession at Dagsion.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B02_m01_002: Then, the nation's reputation hung in the balance,\nbut now we're fighting for our very survival.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B02_m01_003: If we lose here, there's no future for us. Her Majesty\nhas my full faith as we march on the capital!
MID_LGA_2_M04_B02_m01: <BLN>I was in Her Majesty's procession.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B03_m01_001: The mood around camp has been a little more\ncheerful since we gained the support of those gods.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B03_m01_002: Honestly, it might be enough to make me rethink my\nopinions of the Dagdan pantheon.
MID_LGA_2_M04_B03_m01: <BLN>The mood's really changed!
MID_LGV_2_M04_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B04_m01_001: King Bertrand! Such strength and vigor, white hair,\nflowing like a battle standard!
MID_LGV_2_M04_B04_m01_002: Still, I'd love to have seen the dignified young noble\nwith black hair...
MID_LGA_2_M04_B04_m01: <BLN>Such strength and vigor!
MID_LGV_2_M04_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B05_m01_001: Mars used to consider Jurah to be a more fitting\ninterim leader than Solel.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B05_m01_002: But she refused the position and spent several\ncenturies scarcely ever taking the political stage.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B05_m01_003: Yet now that same Jurah has seen fit to act on our\nbehalf... Mars must be overjoyed.
MID_LGA_2_M04_B05_m01: <BLN>Mars must be overjoyed.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M04_B06_m01_001: Someone I knew died in the last battle. The idiot\nthrew his life away to protect an ally.
MID_LGV_2_M04_B06_m01_002: We'd finally gotten to thinking of ourselves as friends\ndespite our different homelands and beliefs...
MID_LGV_2_M04_B06_m01_003: Why now? Damn it...I feel sick.
MID_LGA_2_M04_B06_m01: <BLN>Urgh... That idiot!